This crate (`symphonia-codec-sipr`) is a pure-Rust RealAudio SIPR (Sipro Lab ACELP.net) decoder. It
is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

SIPR has no public specification. The bitstream layout, LSF/gain/pitch decoding, the fixed
codebook, the post-filters and the 16 kbit/s mode follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/sipr.c` and
`sipr16k.c`; the supporting CELP/ACELP routines (LSP to LPC conversion, interpolation, vector
sums, filters) follow `libavcodec/lsp.c`, `acelp_vectors.c`, `acelp_filters.c`,
`acelp_pitch_delay.c` and `celp_filters.c`. The codebook and window tables (`src/tables.rs`,
extracted programmatically) come from `libavcodec/siprdata.h`, `sipr16kdata.h` and
`acelp_vectors.c`. These files are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later.

